 "title": "Tribal Toms",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: rolling, pitched tom drums over a steady kick: a tribal, ritual rhythm, the drums of darker industrial and EBM. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 100. The toms are a single drum (a sine with a small pitch drop) whose PITCH comes from a Sequencer: each step plays a different tom, high to low, and steps switched off are rests. The kick on every beat. A big Reverb.\n\nTweak: the sequencer's step knobs (the tom tunings) and buttons (the rhythm), the tom envelope's DECAY, TEMPO.",
